File 5 of 5: .env.example
1. Exact Repository Path
.env.example
2. Action in GitHub
Replace existing file (.env.example already exists in the repository root).
3. Important Notice on Environment Variables & Security
.env.example is a documentation template committed to GitHub. It contains only safe, non-sensitive placeholders to document the schema of required variables for developers and server deployment.
NEVER put real client secrets, API keys, or private tokens into .env.example or commit a .env file to GitHub.
Real production values must be configured in Vercel:
Open your project on the Vercel Dashboard.
Navigate to Settings → Environment Variables.
Add each production variable for the Production environment (and Preview / Development as needed).
Trigger a redeploy after setting environment variables so the serverless function can access them.
4. Complete File Contents
code
Env
# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.
# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI or Vercel Environment Variables.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# APP_URL: The public base URL where this application is hosted.
# In local dev: http://localhost:3000
# On Vercel: https://care-plus-clinic-rose.vercel.app
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="https://care-plus-clinic-rose.vercel.app"

# Optional local server port (defaults to 3000 if omitted)
PORT="3000"

# GOOGLE OAUTH & GOOGLE WORKSPACE INTEGRATIONS (SERVER-SIDE ONLY)
# Used when enabling real Google Calendar, Google Sheets, and Gmail integrations.
# When not configured, CarePlus operates safely in simulated/demo mode.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com"
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET"

# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI: Must match an Authorized Redirect URI in Google Cloud Console Credentials.
# In local dev: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google/callback
# On Vercel: https://care-plus-clinic-rose.vercel.app/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI="https://care-plus-clinic-rose.vercel.app/api/auth/google/callback"

# OAUTH_STATE_SECRET: Dedicated server-side cryptographic secret used to HMAC-sign
# OAuth state tokens across stateless Vercel serverless instances (preventing CSRF).
# Generate using: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# If not provided, the server falls back to GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET.
OAUTH_STATE_SECRET="YOUR_RANDOM_LONG_HEX_SECRET"

# Optional pre-configured refresh token if using server-level authorization:
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=""

# Google Calendar ID for appointment events (e.g. "primary" or a dedicated clinic calendar ID)
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID="primary"

# Google Sheets Spreadsheet ID for appointment logging (from the spreadsheet URL)
GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID="YOUR_GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID"

# Clinic Notification Email for staff alerts via Gmail
CLINIC_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL="clinic-admin@example.com"
5. How to Save in GitHub Web Interface
Navigate to your repository: https://github.com/kavi930/CarePlus-Clinic.
Click on the .env.example file in the root list.
Click the pencil icon (Edit this file) in the top right corner.
Select all existing text and paste the complete content above.
In the Commit changes box:
Commit message: Update .env.example with Vercel deployment and OAuth state variables
Ensure Commit directly to the main branch is selected.
Click Commit changes.
All 5 Files Are Complete!
Here is the checklist of the 5 files updated for your Vercel deployment:
#	File Path	Action	Purpose
1	api/index.ts	Created	Serverless function entry point wrapping the Express app
2	vercel.json	Created / Replaced	Routes /api/(.*) to serverless backend; rewrites others to SPA index.html
3	server/config.ts	Replaced	Automatic Vercel production URL detection + safe redirect URI generation
4	server/auth/googleOAuth.ts	Replaced	Stateless HMAC-signed OAuth state tokens across serverless lambdas
5	.env.example	Replaced	Complete documentation of all deployment & OAuth environment variables
Next Step to Test on Vercel:
Verify in your Vercel Project Dashboard that a new deployment build has completed for branch main.
In Google Cloud Console (APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client IDs), confirm that https://care-plus-clinic-rose.vercel.app/api/auth/google/callback is listed under Authorized redirect URIs.
In Vercel (Settings → Environment Variables), make sure GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, and OAUTH_STATE_SECRET are configured.
Test by visiting:
https://care-plus-clinic-rose.vercel.app/api/auth/google/url
You should receive a JSON response with { "url": "https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth?..." } instead of a 404!
